I agree that information on lojban must be everywhere. But is it really 
happening ?
I guess we need to revise all the stuff that lojban has accumulated by now 
and place it onto lojban.org
This is not happening on a regular basis.
Lot's of stuff nut it's not easily accessible.
As for facebook, g+ and livejournal you should definitely harness any 
cross-posting tool.
The ideal would be to add Google groups to this cross-posting mechanism too.

On Saturday, January 28, 2012 1:36:32 PM UTC+4, la .lindar. wrote:
>
> This isn't about competing formats. I, Lindar Greenwood, am personally 
> undertaking this effort as a pseudo-BPFK member. I've picked what appear to 
> be the three most popular media and am now pretty much reposting stuff from 
> Lojban-central (IRC and the mailing list) so that the wider community has 
> an idea of what is going on instead of being this completely detached 
> section that has no idea what's going on. So this isn't really a community 
> effort, per se. This is actually semi-official reposting 
> of bureaucratic bullshit from the LLG/BPFK that I'm trying to transmit to 
> all of the people that are pretty much alienated from our community so we 
> can start involving all of the Japanese/Russian/$nonwesternculture people 
> that don't enjoy sitting on IRC all freaking day.

